WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.800
Begin with grain size. Gravel-sized fragments can form breccia

00:00:03.800 --> 00:00:08.940
or conglomerate. Angular pieces identify breccia. As transport abrades

00:00:08.940 --> 00:00:12.860
corners, rounded pieces can form conglomerate. Rounding does not

00:00:12.860 --> 00:00:16.760
establish one unique environment. Sand accumulates and becomes sandstone

00:00:16.760 --> 00:00:20.380
as grains are compacted and cemented. Mineral composition refines

00:00:20.380 --> 00:00:25.220
the name: feldspar-rich sandstone is arkose. Well-sorted quartz sand

00:00:25.220 --> 00:00:27.920
differs from sand with abundant matrix or less resistant

00:00:27.920 --> 00:00:31.940
minerals. Mud settles in quieter conditions and can become

00:00:31.940 --> 00:00:35.200
mudstone. Shale is a mudrock that splits along thin

00:00:35.200 --> 00:00:38.820
layers. To infer the setting, add fossils, bedding, and

00:00:38.820 --> 00:00:42.760
regional relations. Grain size is a starting observation, not

00:00:42.760 --> 00:00:44.320
a complete environmental history.
